==Old English==

===Etymology===
From [[hlaf|hlāf]] + a second element representing a Germanic ''*deigjōn'' ‘kneader’ (compare Old English [[dǣġe]], Old English {{term|dag|dāg|lang=ang}} "dough"). Similar to a [[kenning]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlæːvdiːje/|[ˈɬæːvdiːjə]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=f|head=hlǣfdīġe|pl=hlæfdigan|plhead=hlǣfdīgan}}

# a [[lady]], the mistress of a household.